<!--
    Notification tray icon for the Oracle push channel.

    A status-bar icon is an alpha mask, not a picture: Android discards
    the colours and tints whatever silhouette it finds. So the source
    artwork's two gradient-filled flames survive here as geometry only —
    the outer flame is the body and the inner one is subtracted from it,
    which is why `fillType` must stay `evenOdd`. Flatten the two into a
    single solid shape and the icon turns into an unreadable blob.

    Fitted to 22x22 inside the 24dp viewport, so the flame keeps a 1dp
    margin on every side and the system never clips it. Verified legible
    at 24, 48 and 63 px (the last is 24dp on a 420dpi device).

    Deliberately unlike the launcher icon (pitfalls §13) and a single
    #FFFFFF fill so the tray tint produces clean monochrome.
-->
